  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#dom-lfe-labels\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconsole.assert(labels.length =​=​=​ 0); // the label is no longer the input's labeled control\r\nconsole.assert(input.labels =​=​=​ null);\r\n\r\ninput.type =​ 'checkbox';\r\nconsole.assert(labels.length =​=​=​ 1); // the label is once again the input's labeled control\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe terminology in these comments seems backwards. A **`label`** has a [labeled control](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#labeled-control) (the control being a form control, e.g. an `input`), not vice-versa. (An `input` can **be** a labeled control, but it does not **have** a labeled control.)",
